-- Runtime companion to the compiler test case aggregate_taking_container.
--
-- 'closet' takes garment, and a garment is a bare container, so the classes
-- that might transitively be in the closet are 'garment' and 'object'. The
-- aggregate resolves 'cover' from 'garment', and the generated existance
-- filter must skip the wallet, which is in the shirt but has no 'cover'.
--
-- 3 + 5 = 8, and the wallet must neither contribute nor be read.

The l Isa location
End The l.

The closet Isa object At l
  Container Taking garment.
End The closet.

Every garment Isa object
  Has cover 0.
  Is washed.
  Container
End Every garment.

The shirt Isa garment In closet
  Has cover 3.
  Is washed.
End The shirt.

The coat Isa garment In closet
  Has cover 5.
  Is Not washed.
End The coat.

The wallet Isa object In shirt
End The wallet.

Start At l.
  If Sum Of cover In closet = 8 Then "Ok" Else "not ok" End If.
  If Sum Of cover Is washed, In closet = 3 Then "Ok" Else "not ok" End If.
